--
-- demo\theGUI\theGUI.e
-- ====================
--
--  A new (June 2026) cross-platform GUI for Phix (1/7/26: 8:25pm)
--
--  A cross platform GUI:
--   * works on Windows, Linux (including Raspberry OS[?]), and under pwa/p2js.
--   * Uses fully emulated (carefully copied) controls instead of any native ones.
--   * Uses winAPI directly on Windows, essentially arwen-based but more IUP-like.
--   * Uses GTK on Linux, likewise Raspberry OS, and can be induced to on Windows.
--   * Uses theGUI.js in a browser, a manually hand-crafted drop-in replacement.
--  Uses an IUP-inspired attribute system, although IUP itself is not used at all.
--  Routines are named after Iup, eg gSetAttribute() is like IupSetAttribute().
--
--  Motivation:
--   * Installing IUP on Linux was nowhere near as easy as I hoped it would be,
--     plus there are no prebuilt binaries(/support) of IUP for an ARM machine.
--   * Low-level hiccups, in particular the inability to prevent <Alt x> bleeping,
--     and timing problems triggering unexpected/unstoppable program shutdowns.
--   * The IUP layout is not the best fit for the browser box model, and it is
--     far easier to modify desktop/Phix than Chrome, FireFox, and all the rest.
--   * Much of the work already done in pGUI.js should be easily transferrable.
--   * Likewise much of the IUP documentation should need only minor adjustments,
--     that is eg copy IupButton.htm to gButton.htm and rip out/add a few things.
--   * It should also be reasonable easy to transfer opengl.e by removing both of
--     iup_c_func/proc() and making define_c_func/proc() crash by default. [DONE]
--  Using GTK on Windows almost certainly won't be officially supported, but it
--  should obviously prove rather useful for testing and development purposes.
--
--  Some bits may end up in separate file(s), so they can be auto-transpiled.
--
-- BUGS:
--  Left arrow on a submenu closes it but does not re-highlight the parent menu.
--  <Alt Down> on a gDatePick/gCalendar should open the popup, and <Alt Up> /
--  <Return> should close it. Also add linkup code to gDatePick/gDropdown.exw
--
-- Bug: optionally disable gSetAttribute(edit,{`BGCLR`,`BGHOV`},TG_SILVER) so       [FIXED]
--  you can see hover effects on the main gList, then open theEditor at a small
--  size such as 600x300 such that the main menus will overlap the horizontal
--  scrollbar. When moving about on the menu, hover effects leak through to the
--  latter, but oddly /not/ to the gList, as can be seen by slidng sideways off 
--  the menu and back onto in. If we can figure out why not, then we can apply
--  that same whatever to stopping the unwanted scrollbar effects.
--  AHA: tg_list_hover() is setting LX_HOVLINE, and tg_list_mouseleave() is
--  removing it. In contrast, tg_scrollbar_mousemove() is getting monsba, then
--  redrawing without saving it when != SB_MONLD, and tg_redraw_scrollbars() 
--  re-getting it. So tg_scrollbar_mousemove() needs to save it and redraw
--  use the saved version, and tg_list_mouseleave() clear it instead.
--  Done, works, and replicated for table and tree.
--


