-- Aside: This source is littered with
--
--      if backend==TG_GTK then
--          ...
--      elsif backend==TG_WINAPI then
--          ...
--      elsif backend==TG_JS then
--          --/*
--          <javascript>
--          --*/
--      else
--          ?9/0 -- (unknown backend)
--      end if
--
-- While only a few of those ?9/0 can actually trigger now, mid-way through adding say Qt
--  they should theoretically be helpful to locate "what next to get next demo working".
--
-- Some subtle tricks are used with the above to help ease transpilation to javascript:
-- you may notice I've used "==" above to stop the pre-process stage from messing with
-- it, which only happens when the first three lines of src match this file, and the
-- js branch must be block-commented javascript. Arguably it might actually want phix
-- code instead of js, but if you pen local procedure some_phix_code()...end procedure
-- then "some_phix_code();" is perfectly valid javascript, so do it that way instead.
-- Lastly, generally speaking each/every such construct should have all four branches,
-- see p2js.exw/clip_beeq() for the pre-processing stage.
--

